WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.559 --> 00:00:04.059
(piano music)

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.170
- If I could describe how I felt

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.243
before going to therapy in one word, lost, I think, yeah.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:16.740
- Conflicted.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.573
- Sad.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.090
I mean, I was just really sad.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:21.013
- Chaotic.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.173
- Numb.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:26.940
- It was in October my sophomore year of college.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:31.225
I was at my then girlfriend's house and all of a sudden

00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:34.370
my brain started having this downward spiral.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:37.470
My chest started racing, I was having trouble breathing,

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.650
then the panic attacks kept happening.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.480
When I started going through depression

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.420
and I wasn't my full self,

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.640
I didn't feel like there was anyone I could talk to about it

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.270
because I felt like my friends only wanted to be around me

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:52.690
when I was my 100% goofy, super happy self.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.640
So, I started thinking about going to therapy.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.020
I tried to talk myself out of it a billion times.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:01.340
Therapy is for people who have big, traumatic problems,

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.760
not a 19-year-old who's depressed and can't study.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.690
I kept discounting my own feelings, and so,

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:07.970
thank god I got to go in there

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.280
and talk about these fears with her.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.770
She was like, well, how are you feeling?

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.600
And then suddenly it was just like

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.530
every thought I ever had poured out.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:17.390
When you go through depression or anxiety,

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:20.090
you often think something had to have happened.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:22.960
There had to have been an event and oh, now you're sad,

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.780
but that's not the case.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.233
Sometimes you're just sad.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.810
- My reason for wanting to do therapy

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.730
was partly related to just life goals

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.360
and things that I wanted to get done

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.230
and feeling that there may have been

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:36.780
a little bit of a stagnancy,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.520
and it's been life changing.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.780
One of my larger motivators

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.176
for being open about going to therapy

00:01:42.176 --> 00:01:44.530
is the fact that I am a black man,

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:49.260
and I don't think that, within the community of black men,

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.450
the topic of therapy is talked about very often.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.040
Giving other black men encouragement

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.750
that it is okay and we can do this too,

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:59.820
that also helps us overcome a stigma that we can't,

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:03.010
or we're not allowed to take care of our mental health.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:04.700
There is a privilege for a lot of people.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.700
There is a privilege of having insurance,

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:10.440
and you're not having to pay $150 for every session.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.970
Yeah, the system isn't really set up

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.000
for everybody to have access to that.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:14.993
That's not okay.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.700
- So, I started going to therapy at a relatively young age.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.210
I was around 17 years old.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.460
I was actually diagnosed with anorexia.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:25.087
Around the same times that I was diagnosed with anorexia

00:02:25.087 --> 00:02:27.290
I was also diagnosed with depression.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:32.290
My being gay played a big part in my eating disorder.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.680
It's really easy to feel shitty about your body

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.710
as a guy in an LGBTQ community.

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:40.841
As a recently identified queer person

00:02:40.841 --> 00:02:44.893
with an eating disorder, going to therapy was super helpful,

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.260
it was really essential,

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:49.500
and I don't know what I would've done without that.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:52.620
I know people can think that going to therapy means

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.920
that you're mentally unstable.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.723
I would sort of try to erase those qualms if you can.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:00.550
It is literally just like talking to a friend

00:03:01.664 --> 00:03:05.440
whose job is to just listen to you and talk to you

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.223
and provide objective advice.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.480
- My senior year, I was taking 21 and 24 credit hours,

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:14.560
and I had two very close friends get get killed.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.500
So, I went to therapy and I started to talk to them.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.270
It was a very cathartic feeling

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.540
because it allowed me to grieve.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.630
It was very important for me

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:25.370
to have another black woman therapist.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:28.040
It feels good to be able to speak to a therapist

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.390
and relay certain things

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.450
and they don't think that you're making it up.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.033
It's good to just be like,

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.220
you've been through this too, I'm sure.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:39.279
So, having an older black woman be able to talk to me,

00:03:39.279 --> 00:03:41.780
but also walk me through my healing

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.720
was a very beautiful thing.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.450
Learning to go through the feels.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:50.170
So often we're sort of taught to suppress them

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.453
and keep it moving and act like we're okay.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:54.593
If you're not okay, that's fine.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.360
- I was grieving from having lost my father.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.250
A month after that,

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.870
I lost my grandfather and moved away from my family.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.470
I'd left my job that I loved and I didn't have a job.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.760
It was just hard to even get out of the house.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.570
I was finally like okay, I need to do something for myself,

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:11.900
get off my ass and do something.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.960
It was very helpful for me because I felt like

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.340
I had this person that I was accountable to.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.830
I don't know, everything kind of just changed after that.

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:21.972
Obviously therapy deals with people

00:04:21.972 --> 00:04:25.040
all over the spectrum of mental health.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.555
You don't have to suffer from anxiety

00:04:27.555 --> 00:04:29.830
or depression to go to therapy.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.230
Even if you don't think you benefit,

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.010
even if you don't think you qualify,

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:38.470
even if you think you're super happy and uber blessed,

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:41.473
I think everyone would benefit from therapy.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.470
- Capable, I feel really capable.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:47.497
- Shit, I feel...

00:04:47.497 --> 00:04:48.590
I feel empowered.

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:49.870
- Better and stronger.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:50.720
- Liberating.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.193
- I felt validation.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.840
I think it's the best thing you can do for yourself.

00:04:55.277 --> 00:04:58.110
(uplifting music)

00:05:12.488 --> 00:05:14.329
(squeaking)

